From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:49:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: apple: pmgr-misc: Add the S8000

The S8000 and S8003 (A9) select their combined SoC and memory
performance state in one PMGR register, as the T8010 does: describe it
as a single "soc-ps" region.

[Orchard: from orchard PR #122, commit 5775e3ed; unchanged]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6000-pmgr-misc.yaml        | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6000-pmgr-misc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6000-pmgr-misc.yaml
index e64ca2ce9..001b791dd 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6000-pmgr-misc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6000-pmgr-misc.yaml
@@ -12,12 +12,13 @@ maintainers:
 description: |
   Certain Apple SoCs include additional PMGR power states that are controlled
   via a different "misc" control block. This includes the fabric and memory
-  controller states. On the T8010 (A10) one register selects the combined
-  SoC and memory performance state.
+  controller states. On the S8000/S8003 (A9) and T8010 (A10) one register
+  selects the combined SoC and memory performance state.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
+      - apple,s8000-pmgr-misc
       - apple,t6000-pmgr-misc
       - apple,t6020-pmgr-misc
       - apple,t8010-pmgr-misc
@@ -40,7 +41,9 @@ allOf:
       properties:
         compatible:
           contains:
-            const: apple,t8010-pmgr-misc
+            enum:
+              - apple,s8000-pmgr-misc
+              - apple,t8010-pmgr-misc
     then:
       properties:
         reg:
